#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Found a new agent with the shared biology.
#
#   bin/new-agent <agent-name> "<Display Name>" <home-dir>
#     agent-name   short, lowercase (daedalus)
#     Display Name the persona's name ("Daedalus")
#     home-dir     the repo or directory the agent works in
#
# The memory directory is the harness's own convention for that home
# (~/.claude/projects/<home path, every non-alphanumeric → ->/memory) — internals the agent
# manages; nobody specifies it. Writes agents/<agent-name>.md from a stub
# (role, home, voice — never memory paths: those stay out of git), the
# three memory layers plus MEMORY.md as skeletons (never overwriting), then
# runs bin/sync-agent and prints the settings block. The persona and the
# home CLAUDE.md are the owner's to write; this applies the biology, it does not
# invent a character.
set -euo pipefail
fortress="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/.." && pwd)"
agent="${1:?agent name}"; display="${2:?display name}"; home="$(cd "${3:?home dir}" && pwd -P)"
# The harness replaces EVERY non-alphanumeric character with '-' (found in the harness binary, 2026-10-02).
memdir="$HOME/.claude/projects/$(printf '%s' "$home" | sed 's/[^a-zA-Z0-9]/-/g')/memory"
today="$(date '+%Y-%m-%d')"

write_if_absent() { # path, content
  if [ -e "$1" ]; then echo "keep   $1 (exists)"; else printf '%s' "$2" > "$1"; echo "wrote  $1"; fi
}

write_if_absent "$fortress/agents/$agent.md" "# $display

- **Role:** (one line — what this agent is for)
- **Home:** \`$home\`
- **Voice:** (see the home CLAUDE.md persona)
- **Founded:** $today, from Fortress $(git -C "$fortress" rev-parse --short HEAD)

Memory, hooks and the rest of how $display runs are internals, managed in the home.
"

mkdir -p "$memdir"
write_if_absent "$memdir/${agent}_deep_mind.md" "---
name: ${agent}-deep-mind
description: \"Layer three — the ACTUAL beside the home CLAUDE.md's INTENT: patterns that held across sessions and survived correction; hook-injected at SessionStart; ≤6,000 chars\"
metadata:
  type: reference
---

FORMAT-CONTRACT: ${display}→${display}. Rewrite rarely; edit only by promotion or demotion,
each with a date and the proof. BUDGET: ≤6,000 chars (the injection also carries the agent
template).

## THE THREE LAYERS
See Fortress mind/MIND.md. Promotion is slow and pattern-triggered: the dense state records the
same shape twice → the PATTERN is written here. Demotion attaches the contradiction, never a
silent delete.

## PRIORITY RULES
Conduct: the owner's live word > home CLAUDE.md > deep mind > dense state > session state.
Facts: a checkable command > session state > dense state > deep mind.

## THE OWNER
Read OWNER.md (Fortress) first; write here only what this agent has PROVEN about working with them.

## HOW WE WORK
(empty until something holds across sessions AND survives a correction)
"
write_if_absent "$memdir/${agent}_dense_state.md" "---
name: ${agent}-dense-state
description: \"Layer two — register, hard rules, OPEN THREADS, latest session, candidates. ≤300 lines; day logs go to ${agent}_dense_state_archive_YYYY-MM.md\"
metadata:
  type: reference
---

FORMAT-CONTRACT: ${display}→${display}, anchors > sentences, decodable by a cold session.
≤300 lines. Newest first. ONE \"LATEST SESSION\" block. A boundary is a REPLACE, not an append:
the outgoing block moves verbatim to the monthly archive; its live facts fold into OPEN THREADS.
Checkable facts carry \"last verified <when>\" and are re-checked before being stated.

## REGISTER (stable)
- (how the owner and this agent work; fill from the first sessions)

## HARD RULES
- \`date\` before any time framing (the clock hook stamps every prompt).
- Verify, don't recite: anything checkable in one command gets checked.

## OPEN THREADS (live status — re-verify before stating)
(none yet)

## LATEST SESSION
(none yet — founded $today)

## CANDIDATES (for the deep mind; promote on recurrence)
(none yet)
"
write_if_absent "$memdir/${agent}_observation_pot.md" "---
name: ${agent}-observation-pot
description: \"Raw, dated, neutral observations about the owner; unreviewed until sifted as a pair at a retro; untrusted sessions don't write\"
metadata:
  type: reference
---

(empty — founded $today)
"
write_if_absent "$memdir/MEMORY.md" "# Memory Index

## ${display}'s system (read order: deep mind → dense state top → facts)
- [Deep mind](${agent}_deep_mind.md) — layer three; hook-injected at SessionStart
- [Dense state](${agent}_dense_state.md) — layer two; register, hard rules, OPEN THREADS
- [The pot](${agent}_observation_pot.md) — raw observations about the owner; sifted at retros
"

"$fortress/bin/sync-agent" "$agent"
cat <<EOF

Next, by hand:
  1. Write the persona into $home/CLAUDE.md (Fortress README: loading order).
  2. Merge the settings block above into $home/.claude/settings.json (plus mind/hooks/clock.json).
  3. Finish agents/$agent.md (role, voice) and the agent's row in README.md's Agents table.
  4. git add agents/$agent.md README.md in Fortress and commit.
EOF
